        <p>BOLD- STREET WESLEYAN CHURCH WARRINGTOIf. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY) DECEMBER 17041 At 10 30, Rev. JOHN GUNNELL. At 630. Rev. H. G. ROBERTS M.A. Al! Nvelenme. Hymn Books provided.</p>
        <p>WYCLIFFE HALL, BmveET Et -STRtT, WARRINGTON. MONDAY NEXT, DECEMBER Mu, 1899. LANTERN LF.CTURE ON PAUL KRUGER, Kis Country, People, and War with Great Britain, LIFE AMONG THE BOERS, Br REV. J N. RIDDETTE, Of Haydock. Three years an Outlander. Cbair to he taken at 7.45 by F. MONKS. RSQ • P., C.C. ADMISSION :—Three Pence; Second Seats (by ticket), 6d; Reserved Seats (by ticket), One Shilling. Tickets at Mr. Bee wick's. Buttermarket-street ; Mr, Pei- more, Rylands-street ; Mr. Hawtkorn, 1, Lovely-lane, NVYCLIFFE CIZURCH, BEVitSEY STREET, WAR RINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY) EVENING, DECEMBER 17, CHRISTMAO CHORAL SERVICE. SELECTIONS FRoM AH." SWAIM : Miss F. BOOTH. Miss E. KERSHAW, Mrs. A. BOOTH, and Messrs. A. GRIFFITHS, G. CLAY, jun., and C. A. GOLDTHORPE, INSTRIMENTALISTS :_Messrs. It. H. PEARSON, W. BROWN, A. KN' ,WLES, Mies B. BOUCHIER, Messrs. T. PEPLOW, H. BOND. 11, WHITFIELD. Organ, Mr. F. HICKMAN. Connuarou : W. H. PAYTON, Mug, Bee, Services 6-30. Offertory for Choir. -</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON MUSICAL, S._2CI.ILTY. TO-NIGHT (SATURDAY) 44 14 111FSSIAli." SOPRANO ... MI"S M. BKYNON. CONTRALTO MISS JUANITA JONES. TENOR ... MR. CHARLES SAUNDERS. BASS MR. BANCOCK P,ERPOINT. .11116RUS AND ORCHESTRA OF OVER 200 PERFORMERS. CONDUCTOR ; MR. FRANK H. CROSSLEY. Hon. Orgenist : Mn. J. B. CALDWELL. Leader of OrcheAtra : Mn. R. 11. PEARSON. POPULAR PRICES :-2s. Is. and 6d. Doors open 7.0 p.m. Concert 7.30 p.m. Cirriages 10.15p.m. Early Doors for Tieket-belders only, open at 6 45. W. E. ATKIN. Hon. See.</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON TEMPERANCE FEDERATION.</p>
        <p>GRAND UNITED RALLY IN THE PARR HALL ON TUESDAY EVENING DECEMBER 19TH. SPEAKERSTn VERv REVERE D THE DEAN OF INREFORD. ARC RDEAC( )N MADDEN. and several Local Clergy Ministers and other Gentlemen. THE UNITED CHOIR ef the WARRINGTON BAND OF HOPE UNION Will render a MUSICAL PROGRAMME. HIS WORSHIP THE MAYOR (Alderman Henry Roberts, J P.) will preside. Doors open at 7 to commence at a quarter to 8. ADMISSION: Reserved Chairs. Body of Hall, and Centre Gallery, 6. Rest of the Hall Free. Collection towards expenses.</p>
