      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-12-15_WidnesExaminer_art0002" n="art0002">
        <head>WAR! WAR ! !</head>
        <p>WAR! WAR ! !</p>
        <p>" Pass the hat for your Credit's sake And Pay, Pay, Pay I"—Rildyard Kipling M R. RANDALL'S PATRIOTIC CONCERT. IN AID OF THE WIDOWS AND ORPHANS OF SOLDIERS AND SAILORS (MAYeH's FUND) ON MONDAY EVENING, DECEMBER 18TH. 1899, IN THE ASSEMBLY 100 M. CONSERVATIVE CLUB. UNDEh TUC PATRONAOF THE MAYOR AND MAYORESS, (Alderman H. &amp; Mrs. Roberts). COLONEL E. SPRATT, and Officers ef the Bth and 40th Regiments. LIMIT-COLONEL J. CLARE RIDGWAY and Officers of the 14 Vol. Bat. (P.W.V.) Lane. Regt. and others. The Following Ladles and Gentlemen have kindly given their services : MISS DOROTHY TitUSLOVE will sing " The Minstrel Boy.' MISS A. BA.TE. Contralto, will sing The Battle Prayer." MISS KATE BEESLEY will recite " The Absent-minded Begar." and " Charge of the Light Brigade," The Charge will be blown by Buglers Sergt. Lawless, T. Ince, Hayes &amp; Bramhall. BUGLER T. INCE will play on the English Concertina, " The Mountaineer" and "Cock o th' North." - -</p>
        <p>MR. J. PARKINSON will slug "Let me like a Soldier Fall," and The King's Own." MR. L. AUKLAND will sing "Thy Sentinel am I." and" The Old Brigade.' MR. E. PEARCE, A.L.C.M , will sing "Soldiers of the Queen," and" the Sons of Freedom." THE ORPHEUS QUAR'i ETTE will :lug (by desire), "Comrades in Arms." BAND OF 'THE BTu ixis 40TH REGIMENTS. (by kind permission of Col E, Spratt), will play he Opening Selection. ACCoMPANIsT Mit. PERCY RANDALL. The Audience is particularly requested to join heartily in the singing of the choruses, "Rule Britannia" and "God Save the Queen." Tickets : Front seats, 2s. S. Second :seats, Is. Doors open at 7. Concert at 7-45. Carriages for 9-45 NEWTON-IN-MASERFIFLD URBAN DISTRICT COUNCIL. INSPECTOR OF NUISANCES. The above Council INV tTE APPLICATIONS for the APPOINTMENT of an.;, INSPECTOR OF NUISANCES,for the District of Newton-In-to akerfield. Clindidates must either hold a Certifleats of the Sanitary Institute or undertake to be cerLifici:Led within a period of twelvemonths from the dete of his appointment. The duties of the °Mee will include tho,e of Inspect-r of Common Lodging Houses, Slaughter Houses, Dairies and Mdksbops, ite., and the Collection of Tolls for Street Hawking, and Market Inspector. The appointment which will be made by the Council on the Bth of Jannary 1900 will be subject to the approval of the Local Government Board and will be for a period ot one year :sad so on from year to year (or other perio-: as may be here. . after determined upon) services rendered are satisfa tory. Salary £lOO per annum risiag to £l2O per annum. Applications in ow handwriting stating age, present employment and previous experience (if any) and accom- panied with COPIES of not more than three testimonials of recent date to be forwarded to the undersigned endorsed " Inspector of Nuieances " not later than Wednesday the 20th DECEMBER IE9I. Canvassing the Members .of the Council eiroletly or in- directly will be a diequahhcation. W. W. SU IRLEY, Clerk to the Council, %own Hall, Earlestown, - December 7th, 1899.</p>
        <p>No 1079.</p>
