        <p>.. E Ogden, Warrington _74 74 .G Rowe, Warrington 72 2 74 T Rickers, Warrington 72 2 74 W Masey,Warringtou 66 - 2 68 W Darlington,Peaketh J J Folen, Warrlngton 64 2 66 J Evans, Warrington J Green,, Warrington ........ ..—...62 2 64 A Rutter, Warrington 5B . 2 60 "B J F" Warrington. 54 2 56 A Banner, Warrington ....... —54 54, "C P,"Warrington 4B 2 50 F Wright. Warrington S Tavlin, Warrington 30 2 32 R Albinson, S.-ock!on. Heath 30 30 J. J. Wright, Warrington 16 2 18 W E Kean,Warrington lB 18 W Rigby, Warrington ..... lO 2 12 G Lowe, Warrington. A Gabriel, tockton Heath 4 2 6 I, Broomhall, Earlestown FTrangleton, Warr!ngton ....:. 4 4 NOTlCE.—Solvers who become entitled to a prize -in this competition can, if they desire, have any book on the game of Draughts equal to the value of Sc. instead of cash piNza, by notifying the Draughts Editor.</p>
        <p>In connection with the above competition we may state that we offer a monthly prize of 5s to the competitor who succeeds in placing himself at the head of the solvers' List at the end of the month. Where the prize is awarded the winner's score is cancelled, while the remaining competitors' points go towards the next month's competition. The win- ner may. re-enter the c9mpetition if he chooses commencing again at the bottom of the list. Points are awarded as f(illows : Two for the correct solu- tion of a problem, two for showing a dual solution, two for correcting the author's terms, and hue for each minor correction.</p>
        <p>Intenling competitors may commence at any time.</p>
        <p>SPECIAL NOTICE.</p>
        <p>With Coe adven•-, of the New Year, we propose to alter the mode of scoring points in the above competition. Points will be awarded as follow. : Commencing with Problem No. 66 in our issue of January sth 1900. Two for the correct solution, of the Problem, two for correcting the authors' terms, one for showing a dual key move or a dual solution, and one for showing a dual continuation at any stage of the solution.</p>
