      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-12-15_WidnesExaminer_art0061" n="art0061">
        <head>RUNCORN NOTES.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN NOTES.</p>
        <p>[BY A CORRESPONDENT.] The conduct of the Runcorn Fire Brigade, at the recent fire at Weston, has given rise to general expressions of indignation, and inquiry into it should be the subject of immediate attention. It is the kind of thing—if true—that the Runcorn people will not submit to quietly. The allegation that the Brigade was insufficient and left its post before the fire was extinguished is a very serious one. It was bad enough for the public to have to realise that the Brigade was inadequate for its task; but that was a matter they them-elves could remedy by providing better equipment for the men. When it comes, however, to the charge of general incompetency, a Gtate of affairs truly deplorable is revealed, if the charge is true.</p>
        <p>For some time fire brigades have been under my observation, and the Runcorn Fires Brigade in par- ticular,and I say that it is incompetent for its task. A far more serviceable arrangement than the pre- sent would be a Salvage Corps maintained and equipped by the County Police with good appliances and steam engines located at convenient centres. This body having an organised staff, and maintained by the rates and salvage dues, would accomplish much, as well as be a decided gain in tho matter of method and discipline. The advent of such a body would be welcome, but in any case it is high time something more than the present crude methods and crude engine should be forthcoming.</p>
        <p>It is gratifying to record that the remarks given utterance to last week concerning an allowance of is. a week to a reservist's wife,have been the means of getting the matter notified. It only remains to say there was no blame attaching to the local com- mittee, and a lucid statement of fact righted the matter.</p>
        <p>k laughable incident occorred this week at a Board School not a hundred miles from Runcorn: One of the girl's being absent a messenger was des- patched to the girl's parents with the customary form asking "that the cause of absence he shown." The messenger dol7 delivered the note and received it back apparently filled UP in the orthodox manner Upon the schoolmistress opening it however, she was astonished and considerably annoyed to read the following, under the heading "Cause of absence" :—" Gumboil on her big toe nail (signed) Mrs Nobody." For sometime afterwards a wild scene of consternation raged amongst the teaching staff, and as the joke was supposed to have been perpetrated by the girl's roguish brother a request for his admonition was des- patched to the boy's department of the school: Luckily for the " joker he did not attend there, and the" curtain WAS rung down" to an accom- paniment of threats and invictives hurled at the unknown practical joker.</p>
        <p>The attitude of the County Council in the matter of the sewage from the Ockleston and Highfield Tanneries is one that the public will doubtless note wi.th pleasure as being indicative of a stringent course to be adopted in the prevention of river pollution; and as one that defines the Ship Canal as a river. It is the first step,and a satisfactory one at that, tending in the direction of purifying the Canal and streams within the district. It is to be hoped that the authorities cfmtrolling the sanita- tion of the upper trenches of this great waterway will act as firmly and wisely.</p>
        <p>IMPURITIES 111 THE BLOOD.—"We have seen hosts of lettet from people who have received great benefit from the use os Clarke's Blood Mixture. It cannot be too highly estimated for it cleanses and clears the blood from all impurities. This is a good stintonial from the Family Doctor. which goes on further to say "It is the finest Blood Purifier the science and skill have brought to light, and we can with the utatost confidence recommend it to our subscribers and the public generally." For Scrofula, Scurvy, Eczema, Bad Legs, Skin and Blood Diseases. Pimples and Sores of all kinds. its effects are marvellous. Thousands of Testimonials. Clarke's Blood Mixture is sold everywhere, at 2s. 9d. per bottle. Beware of ,worthless imitations and substitutes. &amp;dvt (4)</p>
