        <p>SUE NRXT " F ERIDAY'S XAMINER," FOR A SPECIAL CHRISTMAS STORY BY GRANT ALLEN, ENTITLED '4 CHRISTMAS ADVENTURE." The following out ine of the story will be perused with interest : Lancelot Saville who is nycling down to a country house to meet his betrothed, Roma Pendleton, meets with an unfortunate accident in a deserted part of the country, and by breaking his leg is exposed to many dangers. He is in danger of dying from starvation, of being robbed by trs.rnps, and finally of being locked up as a bad character. Out of these materials, the author ir.9 woven a very pleasing story, which should be perused with great interest and pleasure lit the family circle. Few writers are better known to fame than the late Mr. Grant Allen. He is celebrated both as a scientist aild a novelist.and so great is the demand for his work that just before his death this year he trebled his prices for stories and still the commissions came rolling in from both sides of the Atlantic. "A Cbriet mas Adventure" will be found one of his best storyettes. We have also pleasure in announcing a MOST INTERESTING ARTICLE ON " CONJURING- FOR OURISTMAS " BY PROFESSOR HOFFMANN, who has the reputation of being the greatest living authority of modern magie, and this article fully sustains his reputation. The subject of the article Is "Spirit Slate-writing Tricks," and it will be embellished by SEVEN ILLUSTRATIONS, L-1 SEE FRIDAY'S 1-I_42(AMINER."</p>
