        <p>WARRINGTON UNION.— ELECTION OF MEDICAL OFFICER for Na. 4or NEWTON DIS TRICT, and for No. 5 or HAYDOCK DISTRICT. NOIICE IS HEREBY Givita that the Guardians of the Warrington Union will on WEDNESDAY. the third day of January, 1900. proceed to the appointment of a Medical Officer for the Newton Medical District of the Union com- prising the Townships of Newton, Burtonwood and Winwick- with-Hulme, at an annual salary of £75. The population of this District is 14892 (1891 census) and the area 8040 acres or thereabouts. Upon the same day the Guardians will also proceed to the appointment of a Medical Officer for the No. sor Haydock District comprising the Township of Haydock —at an anmial salary of £35. The population of this District is 6535 (1891 census) and the area 3103 acres or thereabouts. The Medical Officers Will be required to reside in the respective districts to attend all paupers therein in case of sickness to I provide all medicines (except Quinine,Cod Liver Oil. Morphia Cinchona,-, lodine and Salicyiate of Soda,) and medical and surgical appliances and L.enerally to perform all the duties of I a District Medical Officer as prescribed by the Local Govern- ment Board General Orders. Each Medical Officer will also I be appointed Public Vaccinator for his District. —The appoint- ment will be subject to the Provisions of the Poor Law Officers Superannuation Aet 1896. Candidates for the appoint- ment roust be legally qualified Medical Practitioners. registered under the Medical Act 1858 and must produce their Diplomas, Certificates or Licences to the Guardia us. Applications and Testimonials (not more than 3) with proofs of qualification must be sent to me on or before Saturday the 30th day of December, 1899, and the candidates themselves must attend the meeting of the said Guardians on the said 3rd day of January 1900, at eleven o'elock in the I Forenoon, at the Board Room at the said Warrington Union Workhouse when and where the Election Will take place. Canvassing the Guardians is strictly prohibited and will be deemed a disqualification. Hy Order of the Board JAMBS C. SUTTON, Union Clerk. Bewsey Chambers Warrington, 7th December, 1899.</p>
